==================================================================
STEP-2 LEMMA  (bowed / Salpeter cascade)
Klein antiperiodic involution r -> 1-r on F_{q_3} = F_3
==================================================================
F_3 = {0, 1/3, 1/2, 2/3, 1}

  pair  0 <-> 1    [boundary {0/1,1/1}: redundant with y-periodicity (0~1)]
  pair  1/3 <-> 2/3    [interior: non-redundant antiperiodic flip]
  fixed 1/2              [invariant: no flip]

(a) orbit count = 3 = q_3            -> cascade depth d = q_3
(b) non-redundant flips n = 1
(c) alpha = -q_2 - n/d = -2 - 1/3 = -7/3 = -2.3333
    (observed Salpeter high-mass IMF: -2.35 +/- 0.05; 0.33 sigma)

(d) Selection: orbit_count(F_m) = m only for small m
      m  orbit_count   = m ?
      2            2   match
      3            3   match
      4            4   match
      5            6      no
      6            7      no
      7           10      no

    Holds for m in {2,3,4}; fails at m=5 (phi(5)=4). So depth =
    orbit-count grounds the bowed (d=q_3=3) and clarinet (d=q_2=2)
    cascades, and does NOT ground the deeper Z_6 (d=6, orbit_count
    = 7) or K* (d=14) sectors -- consistent with those being the
    unsupported rungs.
